README.md

# The judging subtree is never part of the platform image. Skill.Suite/Dockerfile does `COPY . .` from the
# repo root, so without this the whole judging layer is baked into a publicly published image - and once a
# session module lives here, that means hidden test suites, reference solutions and local-nuget/*.nupkg.
# Secret hygiene, not build speed.
judging
**/local-nuget

# ...with one exception. Skill.Suite.Application compiles the event protocol in from judging/ as shared source,
# so those .cs files must reach the build. Docker applies an exception by re-including matched paths, so this
# keeps the rest of judging/ excluded while letting the contract through.
#
# Keep this pinned to Protocol/. The rule above exists for secret hygiene, and widening it any further would
# put hidden test suites and reference solutions into a published image.
!judging/Skill.Suite.TestLog/Protocol
!judging/Skill.Suite.TestLog/Protocol/**